$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In the given equation, <span class="italic">k</span> is a constant. If the equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of <span class="italic">k</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 5. Subtracting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53870b6/img_001_372acd75.png" alt="6 x"></span> from both sides of the given equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53870b6/img_002_6374fc88.png" alt="k equals 5"></span>, so for any value of <span class="italic">x</span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53870b6/img_003_63fbc0a8.png" alt="6 x plus k, equals, 6 x plus 5 "></span> if and only if <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/e53870b6/img_004_6374fc88.png" alt="k equals 5"></span>. Therefore, if the given equation has infinitely many solutions, the value of <span class="italic">k</span> is 5.</p>
