that at most 20 items must be ordered, and the second inequality says that the total cost of the order must be at least, not at most, $80.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":4,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959639,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"e744499e","skill_cd":"H.E.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","createDate":1691007959639,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"14928-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"c344bb34-97a3-4a39-95cd-791cb1095a15","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"14928-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">An elementary school teacher is ordering <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"formatted_text font_style:italic \">x</span></span> workbooks and <span class=\"italic\">y</span> sets of flash cards for a math class. The teacher must order at least 20 items, but the total cost of the order must not be over $80. If the workbooks cost $3 each and the flash cards cost $4 per set, which of the following systems of inequalities models this situation?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus y, is greater than or equal to 20, and, 3 x plus 4 y, is less than or equal to 80\n\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus y, is greater than or equal to 20, and, 3 x plus 4 y, is greater than or equal to 80\n\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src