ust be a whole number less than 20.833, the greatest number of batteries that can be used in this circuit is 20.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":8,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959627,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"e8f9e117","skill_cd":"H.E.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","createDate":1691007959627,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"03867-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"9c6d3083-e5ee-4c11-a2d6-0e8801f22b3a","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"03867-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"I equals, V over R\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The formula above is Ohm&rsquo;s law for an electric circuit with current <span class=\"italic\">I</span>, in amperes, potential difference <span class=\"italic\">V</span>, in volts, and resistance <span class=\"italic\">R</span>, in ohms. A circuit has a resistance of 500 ohms, and its potential difference will be generated by <span class=\"italic\">n</span> six-volt batteries that produce a total potential difference of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"6 n\"></span></span> volts. If the circuit is to have a current of no more than 0.25 ampere, what is the greatest number, <span class=\"italic\">n</span>, of six-volt batteries that can be used?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 20. For the given circuit, the resistance <span class=\"italic\">R</span> is 500 ohms, and the total potential difference <span class=\"italic\">V<