figure></figure>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For the linear function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>, the table shows three values of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and their corresponding values of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. If <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis minus 13\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></math>, which equation defines <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6fe38265-331f-4117-976a-c11fd5524ace","content":"<p><math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 5 x minus 4\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"eaffd328-816c-4c7f-a068-7045599a52f5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 5 x plus 7\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"61b9afe2-ddf7-4b3a-ba54-efd36f002bed","content":"<p><math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 5 x plus 9\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e1da0b59-1c38-42e1-a8c6-2bef51833ef9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 5 x plus 20\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["eaffd328-816c-4c7f-a068-7045599a52f5"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. An equation that defines a linear function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> can be written in the form <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> are constants. It's given in the table that when <math alttext=\"x equals negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 0\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals m left parenthesis negative 4 right parenthesis plus b\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals minus 4 m plus b\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Adding <math alttext=\"4 m\"><mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n<mi>m</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> to both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"4 m equals b\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n<mi>m</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"4 m\"><mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n<mi>m</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus 4 m\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></math>. It's also given in the table that when <math alttext=\"x equals negative StartFraction 19 Over 5 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>19</mn>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 1\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"negative StartFraction 19 Over 5 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>19</mn>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus 4 m\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"1 equals m left parenthesis negative StartFraction 19 Over 5 EndFraction right parenthesis plus 4 m\"><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>19</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"1 equals one fifth m\"><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"m equals 5\"><mrow>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus 4 m\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;yields <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 5 x plus 4 left parenthesis 5 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi