</math> must be greater than the corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>. The inequality <math alttext="x less than 22"><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>22</mn></math> indicates that for any solution to the given system of inequalities, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> must be less than <math alttext="22"><mn>22</mn>
</math>. Of the given choices, only choice A contains values of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> that are each greater than the corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> and less than <math alttext="22"><mn>22</mn>
</math>. Therefore, for choice A, all the values of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and their corresponding values of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> are solutions to the given system of inequalities.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The values in this table aren&rsquo;t solutions to the inequality <math alttext="y less than x"><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The values in this table aren&rsquo;t solutions to the inequality <math alttext="x less than 22"><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>22</mn></math>.</p>
